# What NOT to send to the Docker daemon as build context.
#
# Two reasons this file matters more than it looks:
#   1. Secrets. A stray .env in the build context ends up in the `builder` layer via
#      `COPY . .` and is then readable forever with `docker history` / `docker save`, even
#      though the runner stage never copies it.
#   2. Cache and size. node_modules is ~700 MB and .devpg is ~125 MB; shipping either as
#      context invalidates the build cache on unrelated touches and makes every build
#      minutes slower.
#
# WHAT MUST NOT BE ADDED HERE: `public/` and `scripts/`. The KaTeX stylesheet and fonts are
# generated into public/katex/ by scripts/copy-katex-assets.ts during the builder stage, and
# every equation on the site depends on them.

# --- Dependencies: reinstalled inside the image from the lockfile ---
node_modules
**/node_modules
.pnpm-store
.yarn
.npm

# --- Secrets. Never in a layer. ---
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.crt
*.p12
secrets/
**/*.secret

# --- VCS and CI ---
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github

# --- Build output: regenerated inside the image ---
.next
out
build
dist
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# --- Test and tooling artefacts ---
coverage
playwright-report
test-results
blob-report
.playwright
tests/**/__screenshots__
.devpg
.scratch

# --- Infra and docs: not needed to build the app, and editing the runbook must not
#     invalidate the image cache ---
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
docker-compose.yml
docker-compose.prod.yml
infra
docs

# --- Author's working copies of the manuscripts. `content/works/*.md` is what the site
#     builds from; this directory is the raw material and is not read by anything. ---
MY STUFF

# --- Editor / OS noise ---
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
*.swp
*.log
npm-debug.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
tmp-*
.tmp-*
